---
layout: layouts/base.webc
title: Code of Conduct - Cocoboko Studios
description: The Cocoboko community guidelines for a thoughtful, welcoming, and constructive space.
---
<main class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl flex-1 px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
  <article class="prose prose-gray max-w-none prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-indigo-600">
  <h1>Cocoboko Community Code of Conduct</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Welcome</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to the Cocoboko community - which includes our Discord server, the Cocoboko Cafe - a cozy space to chat, chill, and connect around games, creativity, and community. Before joining the conversation, please take a moment to read and respect these guidelines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Be Thoughtful. Be Kind.</h2>
      <p>
        We&apos;re all human here. That means we bring different backgrounds, experiences, identities, and opinions - and that&apos;s a good thing. Treat everyone with <strong>respect</strong>, even when you disagree. Listen more than you talk. Assume good intent. Kindness is not optional.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Zero Tolerance for Harassment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Racist, sexist, or ableist language</li>
        <li>Personal attacks or name-calling</li>
        <li>Unwanted DMs, especially for self-promotion</li>
        <li>Jokes that punch down or make others uncomfortable</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you cross the line, we&apos;ll act, including bans without warning.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Keep It Clean &amp; Constructive</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use appropriate language</li>
        <li>Share content that&apos;s safe for work</li>
        <li>Avoid spam, trolling, or derailment</li>
        <li>Respect content warnings and boundaries</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No Politics, No Drama</h2>
      <p>
        Our community isn&apos;t the place for debating current events or engaging in flamewars. Keep discussion focused on games, creativity, and chill conversation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Promote with Permission</h2>
      <p>
        Sharing your work? Awesome - we love that. But please only post links or self-promotion in the <strong>designated spaces (like channels on our Discord)</strong> and with intention. No drive-by link drops.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Moderators Have Your Back</h2>
      <p>
        Mods are here to help keep the space welcoming. If you see something concerning or feel uncomfortable, please DM a mod (via Discord) or use the report feature on platforms that support it. We&apos;ll listen and act discreetly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>One Rule Above All</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Respect the human on the other side of the screen.</strong><br>
        If you&apos;re ever unsure, err on the side of empathy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p>
        Thanks for being here. Grab a seat, pour your favorite drink, and let&apos;s make something great together.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>
